%% alt: A state diagram with three states. Closed: calls pass through and failures are counted. When failures pass a threshold, it moves to open, where calls fail at once without reaching the dependency. When the cool-down ends, it moves to half-open, where a few trial calls pass. If they succeed it returns to closed; if one fails it returns to open.
%% caption: While open, calls fail fast, so no threads wait on a dependency that is already failing; half-open tests recovery with a few calls.
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  Closed: Closed · calls pass, failures counted
  Open: Open · calls fail at once
  HalfOpen: Half-open · a few trial calls
  [*] --> Closed
  Closed --> Open: failures pass a threshold
  Open --> HalfOpen: cool-down ends
  HalfOpen --> Closed: trial calls succeed
  HalfOpen --> Open: a trial call fails
